    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The UK took its present form in 1922, when the Irish Free State left and Northern Ireland stayed in the union.</li><li>It fought both world wars to victory, standing alone against Nazi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#germany">Germany</a> in 1940, but emerged exhausted and in debt.</li><li>After 1945 it built a welfare state, gave up its empire, joined and then left the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#european-union">European Union</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The country's full name changed only in 1927: from 1922 to 1927 it was still officially the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#united-kingdom-of-great-britain-and-ireland">United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

